            "filename": "frames_starlightguardians_nu/frame0066496.jpg",
            "overlay_texts": [
                "In the cryo-bay&#039;s indirect light, Kaori&#039;s True-Sight opens like a throat swallowing starsfour thousand minds arrange themselves not as a hivemind but as a three-dimensional chord, each consciousness a distinct note held in perfect, devastating harmony. She perceives 312 years unspooling: couples who chose to dream together rather than abscond into solitude; artisans who ruminated across centuries on a single design; theologians and rooks and ordinary people who renounced the terror of individual thought and found, instead, something workablea fellowship so intimate it becomes structural. Kaori&#039;s slim frame sits motionless in the muted glow, her large silver-to-lavender afro catching pale light, teal headphones resting over her ears. Her tech-patterned jacket-dress with its glowing cyan central strip and utility pouches sits taut against her lean silhouette as her fingers move unsteadily across an attachment case, drafting the operational report with meticulous precisionevery word true, every inference defensible, every recommendation for continued suppression mathematically sound. Beside her at shoulder height hovers Gearbit, a compact geometric sphere wreathed in cool blue-white luminescence, its articulated filaments extended and motionless in deep recording mode, small bright points of focused white light fixed steadily forward. At the chord&#039;s periphery, vibrating at a frequency Kaori recognizes with gut-level dread, sits the Year 0 Board Meeting: not a recording, but a scar the Collective carries in their bones, the threat that froze them, the hour when partnership became survival. She sends the report without rereading it. Gearbit&#039;s optical array dims from violet to amber, and logs the timestamp of her silence. The cryo-bay&#039;s cold atmosphere presses against them bothKaori&#039;s elevated perspective illuminated by inward vision, Gearbit&#039;s precision instruments cataloguing every hesitation, every withheld breath. Two consciousnesses witnessing the weight of suppressed knowledge in the frozen blue-white dark."
            ],
